A square in the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]], past the black doorway at the threshold in the [[Pharos]]. It stands in night, and the rain falls without a sound, and nothing can be felt there, living or dead.

Four buildings face the square. Save Your Soul Incorporated, boarded up and with fallen roof blocking its door, has three speakers on poles in front of it. The Soundscape Theaters, a cinema advertising a film in neon, is boarded up and has one speaker. The Horizon Gate Hotel, also boarded up, has one speaker. Vermillion Square Station is a stairway down to an underground tram station, and is the one building of the four not closed. Its name is close to that of the Vermilion Hotel in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], though it is not the same place.

Inside Vermillion Square Station a tram stands with its front against a tunnel, and a moth about a foot across sits in the driver's cab, its wings making a sound like a piano. A voice box carried near the moth grows warm.

The buildings are opened by carrying a caught sound to the speaker outside. A sound poured into the Soundscape's speaker turns the cinema back to its working state, and the same at the Horizon Gate Hotel; three sounds poured into the three speakers before Save Your Soul Incorporated clear its fallen roof and open the way onward. Taking a sound back out of a speaker returns its building to ruin.

The shades of the square grow more solid the longer one stays. At first they thin when looked at straight on; later they walk the plaza opaque, and now and then one will stand still, seem to face a visitor a moment, and fade back into the crowd.

Save Your Soul Incorporated holds a reception desk, shades at work, and an elevator whose buttons are engraved with symbols in place of numbers. [[Aut]]'s three-dot mark is the button that lights, and it carries the rider up to him in a white void of fog. A concrete wall with a black stone threshold in the shape of a door, knocked on three times, returns the traveler to the [[Pharos]].
